orridor itself - and it stops at 18:26:14, 2186 s before the trip ended. The fare breakdown's erp_gantries is null, so no charged gantry places the car off-corridor. The driver's statement confirms the KPE, again the optimal corridor, and admits no diversion. The trip record's 21.2 km is a copy of the impaired trace, as its own admissibility note concedes. So nothing independent carries the distance fact.\n\nThe result. POL-RD-07(iii) and POL-RD-10(3) require ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION where the trace is impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) and no independent corroboration of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) names exists: the absence of proof is a data failure, not a finding for the driver. POL-RD-01's default of NO_ACTION does not apply, because the reading that fails the gate is itself an artefact of the gap. Escalation is terminal: no amount is refunded, no amount is collected, and the SGD 10.00 stays held.\n\nConfidence. The deciding distance fact is carried by EV-GPS-00110 alone at weight 0.39; the trip record copies it and the fare ledger is not independent, so nothing raises the cap under POL-GEN-02(2). Confidence is 0.39, below the 0.70 floor, which independently trips POL-RD-10(1).\n\nWhat would resolve it. An ERP gantry itemisation for this trip (gantry name, coordinates and entry time) showing whether the car crossed gantries the KPE/ECP optimal route does not use; or a GPS export with fixes inside the 18:35-18:42 tunnel stretch; or a driver admission of the route actually driven. Under POL-GEN-04 an appeal may add exactly this kind of record-type evidence.\n\nThe driver's points. Your point that the measured excess (2.8 km, 15.22%) fails the POL-RD-01 gate is correct as far as it goes, but it cannot be turned into NO_ACTION: the measurement is taken on an impaired trace, and POL-RD-07(iii) says the outcome is ESCALATE, not NO_ACTION. Your points that the trip record is not an independent source, that the billed distance is not corroboration, that the rider has shown no independent source, that the chat is consistent with the optimal corridor, and that 15.22% is not a material deviation (below 50% and 8.0 km) are all accepted. Your point on ERP is accepted: there are no gantry lines at all, and the SGD 3.00 matches the trip record's own optimal-route ERP of 3.00, so no billing-integrity refund arises and no POL-RD-09(4) referral is made. Your observation that the impaired-trace branch produces ESCALATE is also accepted. No POL-RD-06(c) referral is made: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 744, so no pattern exists.\n\nThe rider's points. Your points that the trace is impaired for policy (428 s gap, weight 0.39), that the chat supplies no corroboration, that the fare ledger cannot carry the point (erp_gantries null; the charged distance is a copy of the trace), and that the trip record is not an independent source are all accepted. Your point that no extra corroboration burden attaches under POL-RD-08 is also accepted: deviation_claims_60d is 1, below the threshold of 4, and the profile fields are context only under POL-GEN-01.\n\nPrecedent. Earlier cases on these clauses ended PARTIAL_REFUND; what separates this one is that the only distance measurement is an impaired GPS trace with no POL-RD-07(ii) independent source, so no refund can be computed and POL-RD-10(3) applies instead."
